# uv/tooling runtime dirs. These exist by tool design inside a uv project and
# are tolerated locally, but a TRACKED .venv or tool cache is a hard violation
# of the repo's hidden-file law (AGENTS.md, Rico ruling 2026-08-17).
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Never commit real credentials or a local taxonomy/ledger. Config and data
# live in the OS-standard user dirs (see paths.py), never in the repo.
.env
*.jsonl

# The synthetic voice corpus is generated data, byte-reproducible from the
# seed recorded in its MANIFEST.json. Regenerate, never commit:
#   cd scripts && uv run python -m voice_corpus.generate
scripts/voice_corpus/corpus/

# Built kit zips. They are BUILD OUTPUTS of this one codebase (#107 ruling:
# tiers are not separate repos), reproducible from a tagged commit by
#   uv run python scripts/packaging/build_zips.py --tier all
# so the artifact is never the record -- the commit is.
dist/
# dist-ci/ is the same output under the name CI builds into, so a local
# reproduction of the workflow leaves no untracked artifact behind.
dist-ci/

# secrets/ is an ALLOWLIST: real values can never be committed by forgetting a
# blocklist entry. Only the example and the README are tracked.
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example.json
!secrets/README.md

# Install transcripts (install.sh / install.ps1). Per-machine records, never tracked.
logs/
